From: Emir Beganovic <beganovic.emir@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 09:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] bus: mhi: host: destroy remaining child devices before freeing channels

mhi_unregister_controller() frees mhi_cmd, mhi_event, and vfree()s
mhi_cntrl->mhi_chan without first removing any child MHI devices still
attached under mhi_cntrl->mhi_dev->dev. If a controller driver unregisters
MHI while a client device (such as mhi0_IPCR bound to qcom_mhi_qrtr) is
still present, that client remains bound and active with dangling pointers
into the unmapped mhi_chan vmalloc region.

Destroy any remaining child MHI devices after draining hiprio_wq and
before freeing the controller command, event, and channel arrays. When
mhi_power_down() has already removed all children this is a no-op.

Signed-off-by: Emir Beganovic <beganovic.emir@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/bus/mhi/host/init.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/bus/mhi/host/init.c b/drivers/bus/mhi/host/init.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/bus/mhi/host/init.c
+++ b/drivers/bus/mhi/host/init.c
@@ -1071,6 +1071,7 @@ void mhi_unregister_controller(struct mhi_controller *mhi_cntrl)
 		sysfs_remove_file(&mhi_dev->dev.kobj, &dev_attr_trigger_edl.attr);
 
 	destroy_workqueue(mhi_cntrl->hiprio_wq);
+	device_for_each_child(&mhi_dev->dev, NULL, mhi_destroy_device);
 	kfree(mhi_cntrl->mhi_cmd);
 	kfree(mhi_cntrl->mhi_event);
 
